xnu 0409: power the port down before a reset to fastboot

`reboot` from the ring, and the watchdog that stands in for it, both reach
ABL's fastboot and the host then sees no USB device at all: no fastboot, no
ring, and Windows lists nothing new on the port, so the only way out is the
hardware keys. The port is left in the state XNU had it in -- eUSB2 PHY
enabled, repeater powered -- and the bootloader's own enumeration does not
recover from that, while a cold start, where both are off, always enumerates.

So the reset path clears EUSB2_HS_PHY_COMMON0.PHY_ENABLE and votes the
repeater's rails (PM8350 S10 1.8 V, L2 3.072 V) off, then waits 20 ms. ABL
powers the repeater itself when it finds it silent (0313 votes the same two
rails for the cold-boot case), so the boot that follows is not left without
the part.

The PHY write is guarded: a boot whose gadget never came up returns earlier
from mondrian_usb_stop(), and an unclocked block reads 0x09090909.

--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_usb.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_usb.c
@@ -3464,6 +3464,33 @@ mondrian_usb_stop(void)
 	}
 	printf("MONDR USB: stopped before reset (DCTL 0x%08x DSTS 0x%08x after %d ms)\n",
 	    dwc_rd(DCTL), dwc_rd(DSTS), i);
+	/*
+	 * Hand the port back the way a power-on leaves it. A warm reset keeps
+	 * the eUSB2 PHY enabled and the repeater powered in the state XNU left
+	 * them, and the bootloader's fastboot then never enumerates: the host
+	 * sees no new device at all and the phone has to be power-cycled by
+	 * hand (measured on every reset from this kernel). ABL powers the
+	 * repeater itself on a cold start -- 0313 votes the same two rails when
+	 * it finds the part silent -- so dropping them here cannot leave it
+	 * unpowered for the next boot.
+	 *
+	 * The PHY's registers only answer while the block is clocked; a boot
+	 * that never brought the gadget up returns above, and 0x09090909 is
+	 * what an unclocked block reads back as.
+	 */
+	{
+		vm_offset_t phy = ml_io_map(EUSB2_PA, PAGE_SIZE_4K);
+
+		if (phy != 0 && usb_rd(phy, EUSB2_HS_PHY_COMMON0) != 0x09090909u) {
+			/* PHY_ENABLE|RETENABLEN off */
+			eusb2_mask(phy, EUSB2_HS_PHY_COMMON0, 0x9u, 0);
+		}
+		(void)mondrian_rpmh_rail("smpb10", 1800, 0);
+		(void)mondrian_rpmh_rail("ldob2", 3072, 0);
+		delay(20000);
+		printf("MONDR USB: port powered down before reset (phy %s)\n",
+		    phy != 0 ? "disabled" : "unmapped");
+	}
 }
 
 #endif /* ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_MONDRIAN */
